<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia's giant new radar in Kaliningrad raises alarm in NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c77e8e5f215c182ea77b318b5a7adc2eeed7fe5a9498c46af125093bb15f1b1</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815--4cdeadba9801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is nearing completion of what experts think is a giant radar complex in Kaliningrad, capable of monitoring much of Europe. Experts warn the project could intensify the military standoff between Moscow and NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethnic Germans in Kazakhstan face legacy of the Soviet Union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0232be9b39d9580c3b85de820e4582d8bcae45e8c81254c3d1feec734c585b80</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048--09fc50df10b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kazakhstan is struggling to deal with the legacy of the Soviet dictatorship. Some 85 years ago, Stalin deported hundreds of thousands of people: Some 400,000 ethnic Germans living in the USSR were sent to Kazakhstan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Biological weapons: The weaponization of disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:247d65b56e2132c8d4419f9b4a072fa97de86c74f3b81bf69ef268994a96fc24</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T12:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/biological-weapons-the-weaponization-of-disease/a-79819662--554c8f7269e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/biological-weapons-the-weaponization-of-disease/a-79819662?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Biological weapons are prohibited under international law. But new developments in biotech and AI are a cause for concern. DW addresses some of the most important questions about their history, risks, and control.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump loses allies after elections in Serbia and Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7dca55cbdddf2ec4a8e8ae5976cab5d63ec6bd4a5ec80bbfea0349617bde277</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-loses-allies-after-elections-in-serbia-and-brazil/a-79812075--1fdc38eaf775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-loses-allies-after-elections-in-serbia-and-brazil/a-79812075?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro failed to gain power, Aleksandar Vucic was voted out of office, and even Benjamin Netanyahu's position has weakened. An unhappy US President Trump is crying electoral fraud.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FBI says North Korea behind $6 billion Binance crypto theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5923cbf7e923c7d705aa53b19bc1d1816777cf1934f2433d2359a6bebece5f6f</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998--ddc7ca6650b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The FBI said the theft was tied to "malicious cyber activity" by an entity known as TraderTraitor, the same actors behind a $1.5 billion Bybit hack last year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia after Vucic: The winners are losing patience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12fd5954984ba6fa348357db4eba5fdf258520c4c4241f91897e092b16a0925a</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586--7cebe42bf331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Student List's election victory, Aleksandar Vucic's power apparatus is disintegrating. People want justice as soon as possible. But the losers still hold sway in the judiciary and administration.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34b55c55097fde049c9dc6206180084f9757448ac72afb4bb497ec8b377df875</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian PM Mark Carney discusses talks with the EU, overdependence on the US and how to deal with Donald Trump in a DW interview.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:264c25ede4f9dd1beb818ad1785c08e30497e2bcfbf1e1aa9dca91f33a081589</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-do/a-79811469--a55bfac7d94c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-donald-trump-in-a-dw-interview/a-79811469?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Mark Carney tells DW that Canada is seeking closer EU ties to "diversify and deepen" partnerships beyond the Americas. Despite German pushback, he said he favors the all-new term "associate membership."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling, power, profit: Irregular migration out of eastern Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b196ecd45f0efe31de40e8b402efe04b92f62d2e7a09dfbaa468040d0d0ad3b</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-s/a-79808822--583a8979ee7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-power-profit-irregular-migration-out-of-eastern-libya/a-79808822?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">There is currently more irregular migration between eastern Libya and Crete, Greece. It's raising questions as to what connects people smugglers with powerful militias in eastern Libya and then in turn, Europeans.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fefe52406154beb62e5dbc9d8dba80c590486b53cbc5ce751c3a8c0fa807aa1d</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
